    {
      "path": "notes/STAGE_A_711640_PROOF_LEDGER.md",
      "line": 98,
      "text": "The unavailable third-moment archive memo is also no longer needed for its two"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 11,
      "text": "(\\mu_1,\\mu_2,\\mu_3,\\mu_4)"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 24,
      "text": "\\mu_3=r,\\qquad"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 98,
      "text": "### If the third moment is exact"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 118,
      "text": "If \\(q\\le13/4\\), the third moment only needs to be slightly below 2."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 129,
      "text": "\\boxed{\\mu_3\\ge1.995,\\qquad \\mu_4\\le3.25}"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 136,
      "text": "The exact budget lets us trade a weaker third-moment estimate against a weaker"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 150,
      "text": "\\liminf \\mu_3(T)\\ge 2-\\delta_3,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1B_ROBUST_MOMENT_REGION.md",
      "line": 176,
      "text": "> prove \\(\\mu_3\\ge1.995-o(1)\\) and \\(\\mu_4\\le3.25+o(1)\\),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 27,
      "text": "\\mu_3=2,\\quad"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 60,
      "text": "\\mu_3\\ge2-\\delta_3,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 65,
      "text": "Expanding \\(P^2\\) shows that the coefficient of \\(\\mu_3\\) is \\(-7/3\\) and"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 95,
      "text": "\\mu_3\\ge1.996,\\qquad"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 130,
      "text": "Therefore we do **not** need to prove the exact sine-process third moment to"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 133,
      "text": "We can lose four thousandths in the third moment and still cross the line,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 142,
      "text": "\\liminf \\mu_3(T)\\ge1.996,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP70_1C_EXPLICIT_POLYNOMIAL_WITNESS.md",
      "line": 154,
      "text": "> separate lower estimate keeps \\(\\mu_3\\ge1.996-o(1)\\)?"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP71_JOINT_MAJOR_DENOMINATOR.md",
      "line": 32,
      "text": "For the third bound put g=gcd(b1,b2). Prime by prime,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP71_M3_ARCHIVE_RECONSTRUCTION.md",
      "line": 11,
      "text": "\\mu_3\\to2"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP71_M3_ARCHIVE_RECONSTRUCTION.md",
      "line": 98,
      "text": "After division by the third-moment normalization"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP71_M3_ARCHIVE_RECONSTRUCTION.md",
      "line": 273,
      "text": "\\boxed{\\mu_3\\to2}."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP71_UNIFORM_GAMMA_TAIL_THEOREM.md",
      "line": 299,
      "text": "4. the third-moment input used by the degree-two consumer."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP83_RS_BARRIER_MATCH.md",
      "line": 46,
      "text": "For lambda in (1/2,1), this permits at most k=3; C26 explicitly remarks that the odd third moment does not improve the positive-index bound."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_CENTERED_M4_SCALAR_GATE.md",
      "line": 34,
      "text": "    tau(P_R^3)=o(1)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_CENTERED_M4_SCALAR_GATE.md",
      "line": 42,
      "text": "    mu3=1+3v_R+o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_DIRECT_SIGNED_RESTRICTED_CORRELATION_ATTACK.md",
      "line": 107,
      "text": "All moments use the SAME section. The inherited lower inputs are mu1,mu3=o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_CHRISTOFFEL_CENTERED_LEDGER.md",
      "line": 72,
      "text": "        +81188760 mu_3^c"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_CHRISTOFFEL_CENTERED_LEDGER.md",
      "line": 98,
      "text": "    mu_3^c=0,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_CHRISTOFFEL_CENTERED_LEDGER.md",
      "line": 171,
      "text": "    mu_3^c=o(1)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_CHRISTOFFEL_CENTERED_LEDGER.md",
      "line": 269,
      "text": "together with the already-developed controls on mu2, mu3 and the quantitative"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_LOWER_MOMENT_COLLAPSE.md",
      "line": 14,
      "text": "The fixed-band degree-three sign-balance / unique-factorization gate removes the P_R^3 term, equivalently preserving the local identity O3(0,+u,-u)=O2(+u,-u). Hence"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_BAND_LOWER_MOMENT_COLLAPSE.md",
      "line": 17,
      "text": "    mu3(H_R)=1+3v_R+o(1)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_R_ARITHMETIC_FILTERED_MOMENT_TRANSFER.md",
      "line": 55,
      "text": "| Lower centered gates | center at 1, full prime-pair variance near 1/3, aggregate third moment removal | Center at 1 is lost when L/log T does not tend to 1; the original aggregate third gate is not a new high-product theorem |"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_R_ARITHMETIC_FILTERED_MOMENT_TRANSFER.md",
      "line": 214,
      "text": "close at that long cutoff; previously claimed aggregate third-moment gates"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_FIXED_R_ARITHMETIC_FILTERED_MOMENT_TRANSFER.md",
      "line": 216,
      "text": "all degrees through six, including centered third PRIME moment, are covered."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_JOINT_GAUSSIAN_MEHLER_MASTER_LAW.md",
      "line": 64,
      "text": "The extension of Bernoulli invariance to the COMPILED observable is direct: condition on its Mehler noises, replace the shared centered scalar coefficient of each B_p, and match its first two moments. The uniform third directional bound from WP84_COMPILED_MEHLER_PRIME_LINDEBERG yields error at most"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_M4_FREE_ROBUST_CUBIC_R6000.md",
      "line": 95,
      "text": "    mu3^c(H_R)=o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_M4_FREE_ROBUST_CUBIC_R6000.md",
      "line": 301,
      "text": "    mu3^c=o(1)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_M4_FREE_ROBUST_CUBIC_R6000.md",
      "line": 354,
      "text": "mu1^c=o(1), mu3^c=o(1), mu2^c>=1/3-2/(pi^2 R)+o(1), and"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_MATCHED_QUARTIC_MAJORANT.md",
      "line": 117,
      "text": "    mu3=2,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_MATCHED_QUARTIC_MAJORANT.md",
      "line": 203,
      "text": "    mu3 >= 2-delta3,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_MATCHED_QUARTIC_MAJORANT.md",
      "line": 315,
      "text": "- the mu3 reconstruction is already on the branch;"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_MATCHED_QUARTIC_MAJORANT.md",
      "line": 352,
      "text": "    mu3(H_R) >= 2-o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_NON_GAUSSIAN_C5_C6_FIRST_STRIKE.md",
      "line": 71,
      "text": "    mu1^c=o(1), mu3^c=o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_NON_GAUSSIAN_C5_C6_FIRST_STRIKE.md",
      "line": 76,
      "text": "source interface. In particular a scalar third-moment gate is not a tensor"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_NON_GAUSSIAN_C5_C6_FIRST_STRIKE.md",
      "line": 158,
      "text": "    mu2=1/3, mu3=0, mu4=1/4, mu5=1/36,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_NON_GAUSSIAN_C5_C6_FIRST_STRIKE.md",
      "line": 322,
      "text": "| 5: {3,2} | 10 | mixed connected triple and pair; not erased by scalar mu3=o(1) |"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_R400_FILTERED_CONNECTED_KERNEL.md",
      "line": 446,
      "text": "5. selected-section first/third moment gates used by the centered quartic."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_R400_FILTERED_SHARP_REPAIR.md",
      "line": 108,
      "text": "| Same \u00a7\u00a78\u20139 and FIRST_RECORD_ASSEMBLY \u00a7\u00a72\u20135 | Full centered quartic trace | w400<=0.266329, v400<=1/3, first/third moments o(1) | Fourth 593/2000; variance 213/1000; see complete polynomial below |"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_R400_FILTERED_SHARP_REPAIR.md",
      "line": 350,
      "text": "third-moment gates. They are not automatically implied by the fourth bound."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_R400_FILTERED_SHARP_REPAIR.md",
      "line": 423,
      "text": "with Pair4,T,400 <=0.266329+o(1), the first/third moment gates, and the"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_RESOLVENT_KILL_GATE_2026_10_05.md",
      "line": 3594,
      "text": "    mu1>=1-d1, mu2<=4/3+d2, mu3>=2-d3, mu4<=13/4+d4,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_RESOLVENT_KILL_GATE_2026_10_05.md",
      "line": 3616,
      "text": "    mu3=1+3v_R+o(1)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_RESOLVENT_KILL_GATE_2026_10_05.md",
      "line": 3639,
      "text": "Thus the remaining first-strike fallback no longer needs separate mu1/mu2/mu3 estimates; it needs one one-sided fixed-band fourth-moment bound."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_ROBUST_CUBIC_HS_SQUARE_TRANSPORT.md",
      "line": 58,
      "text": "    ell_T=c1 mu1+c3 mu3+c2(mu2-1/3)."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_ROBUST_CUBIC_HS_SQUARE_TRANSPORT.md",
      "line": 63,
      "text": "mu1,mu3=o(1), mu2>=1/3-2/(pi^2 R)+o(1), hence"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_ROBUST_CUBIC_HS_SQUARE_TRANSPORT.md",
      "line": 456,
      "text": "at each of +/-t and remaining mass at 0 has mu2=1/3, mu1=mu3=mu5=0,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_SHARED_CARRIER_JET_RANK_AND_MIXED_DEGREE_INTERSECTION.md",
      "line": 106,
      "text": "      +(2*pi*i*lambda)^3*mu3/6."
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_SIGNED_NEAR_PRODUCT_CELL_DECOMPOSITION.md",
      "line": 37,
      "text": "Thus c4=0. Using the frozen SAME-section lower inputs mu1,mu3=o(1),"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_HOSTILE_AUDIT_AND_BALANCED_PAIR_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 277,
      "text": "does not provide that bound. The inherited scalar third-moment aggregate,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_HOSTILE_AUDIT_AND_BALANCED_PAIR_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 279,
      "text": "separate conditional consumers. In particular scalar mu3=o(1) does not"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_SIGNED_ARITHMETIC_THEOREM_OR_OBSTRUCTION.md",
      "line": 275,
      "text": "inequality (11) for the source. Scalar third-moment, full-to-band,"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_SOURCE_MATCHED_ARITHMETIC_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 264,
      "text": "triple correlation. Nor does scalar mu3=o(1) erase these differently weighted"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_SOURCE_MATCHED_ARITHMETIC_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 284,
      "text": "does not itself bound an aggregate prime-weighted third moment. Summing it"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_SOURCE_MATCHED_ARITHMETIC_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 286,
      "text": "audit already treats scalar mu3 as an inherited conditional input at the"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_STRICT79_SOURCE_MATCHED_ARITHMETIC_REDUCTION.md",
      "line": 290,
      "text": "above needs more than a scalar third-moment statement even if that scalar"
    },
    {
      "path": "notes/WP84_THEOREM_AWARE_DEGREE6_CONSUMER_DESIGN.md",
      "line": 234,
      "text": "Frozen moments are mu0=1, mu1=mu3=0, mu2=1/3, mu4=1/4, mu5=1/36,"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 11,
      "text": "(mu0,mu1,mu2,mu3,mu4)=(1,1,4/3,2,13/4),"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 19,
      "text": "If mu3 >= 2-d3 and mu4 <= 13/4+d4, then because the mu3 coefficient is"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 37,
      "text": "mu3 = F(2)"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 44,
      "text": "    + 2*a*b*mu3"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 57,
      "text": "# mu3 >= 1.996 = 499/250, mu4 <= 13/4."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_explicit_polynomial_witness.py",
      "line": 69,
      "text": "print(\"example_mu3_lower =\", F(499,250))"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 9,
      "text": "  mu3 = r"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 59,
      "text": "    (F(0), F(1,100), \"exact-mu3, mu4=3.26\"),"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 60,
      "text": "    (F(1,1000), F(1,100), \"mu3>=1.999, mu4<=3.26\"),"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 61,
      "text": "    (F(4,1000), F(0), \"mu3>=1.996, mu4<=3.25\"),"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 67,
      "text": "print(\"q_threshold_if_mu3_exact =\", dec(Q70_AT_R2))"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/wp70_moment_region_exact.py",
      "line": 68,
      "text": "print(\"allowed_mu4_excess_if_mu3_exact =\", dec(Q_SLACK_AT_SINE))"
    },
    {
